(:UPSTREAM-DECISION-LEDGER :VERSION 1 :DECISIONS
 ((:ID "e5db10019c8b6eb0" :COMMIT "58a2b2c66f0f5a0900a32910e5991e7d1833d9ed" :SUBJECT "hyperbook-fedwiki/fedwiki.lisp::function:make-fedwiki" :KIND
   :DEFER :STATUS :PROPOSED :RATIONALE
   "Do not adopt the line as it is, and do not decide between usocket:ns-error and the explicit condition classes here. The upstream line has no place in the fork: the handler list that it changes now stands in INITIALIZE-FEDWIKI, which replaced the inline thread of MAKE-FEDWIKI. For the three name-service conditions that the SBCL backend of usocket raises, the two choices behave the same; they differ only for NS-UNKNOWN-ERROR, which the backend never raises and which cannot be printed. Which choice the fork follows is for the maintainers, with upstream's choice in view."
   :EVIDENCE
   ((:TEXT
     "Upstream 58a2b2c replaces usocket:ns-host-not-found-error by usocket:ns-error in the type list of the second handler-case of MAKE-FEDWIKI, the one that protects FETCH-SITEMAP and FETCH-PLUGIN-DATA."
     :STATUS :SOURCE-OBSERVED :BASIS
     ("docs/upstream-intake/evidence/58a2b2c66f0f5a0900a32910e5991e7d1833d9ed.lisp-data" "git diff 9f919fc 58a2b2c in the upstream repository"))
    (:TEXT
     "The definition changed, not its first handler: of the two handler-case forms in MAKE-FEDWIKI, the first (protecting USOCKET:SOCKET-CONNECT, clauses connection-refused-error and ns-host-not-found-error) is the same before and after; only the second changed."
     :STATUS :MECHANICALLY-DERIVED :BASIS ("HANDLER-PROFILES of the before and after text of the recorded evidence"))
    (:TEXT
     "In the fork the changed type list stands in INITIALIZE-FEDWIKI (hyperbook-fedwiki/fedwiki.lisp), not in MAKE-FEDWIKI: the situation is :REPLACED. The upstream hunk does not apply to the fork's file."
     :STATUS :MECHANICALLY-DERIVED :BASIS
     ("SITUATION-OF over the fork's source" "git apply --check of the upstream diff (docs/upstream-intake/evidence/58a2b2c/pr15-provenance.txt)"))
    (:TEXT
     "With the real resolver in an empty network namespace, upstream 58a2b2c survives a try-again or no-recovery condition in the site-map step and ends the process in the first connection attempt; the fork at dreyeck.ch ends the process in both."
     :STATUS :SOURCE-OBSERVED :BASIS
     ("docs/upstream-intake/evidence/58a2b2c/pr15-matrix.tsv (RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15 @7d1adce0, docs/fedwiki-dns-failure/upstream-comparison/evidence/matrix.tsv)"))
    (:TEXT
     "NS-UNKNOWN-ERROR cannot be printed (no applicable method for USOCKET-REAL-ERROR), so a status of that class makes SITEMAP-SNAPSHOT signal; a handler on the parent class NS-ERROR would store such a status."
     :STATUS :SOURCE-OBSERVED :BASIS ("docs/upstream-intake/evidence/58a2b2c/pr15-snapshot-unknown.txt"))
    (:TEXT
     "Explicit classes are kept in the open change for the fork because the list names specific operational failures and the contract rejects an added NS-ERROR; upstream chose the parent class. Switching would be one list entry and a status view that survives an unprintable condition."
     :STATUS :DESIGN-INFERENCE :BASIS ("RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15, docs/fedwiki-dns-failure/upstream-comparison/README.md (sha256 915876e4...)"))
    (:TEXT "Other usocket backends than SBCL's may raise NS-UNKNOWN-ERROR; not checked." :STATUS :WORKING-HYPOTHESIS :BASIS ("none")))
   :REQUIRED-MIGRATION
   "None for ownership: the definition stays a reusable library extension in hyperbook-fedwiki/fedwiki.lisp until upstream has a seam for it (docs/hyperdoc-upstream-boundary.md). The fork's own handler change is RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15, a draft."
   :VERIFICATION
   ("RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15: check-initialize-fedwiki-dns-change in dreyeck/tests/hyperdoc-library-delta.lisp (not on dreyeck.ch yet)"
    "RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15: docs/fedwiki-dns-failure/upstream-comparison/run-matrix.sh"
    "dreyeck/hyperdoc/library-tests (red at the base for other reasons: RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#17)")
   :PROPOSED-BY "Claude, from the analysis of RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15")
  (:ID "4ab5f725a963d41b" :COMMIT "58a2b2c66f0f5a0900a32910e5991e7d1833d9ed" :SUBJECT
   "hyperbook-fedwiki/fedwiki.lisp::function:make-fedwiki#first-attempt-handler" :KIND :PREPARE-UPSTREAM-CONTRIBUTION :STATUS :PROPOSED :RATIONALE
   "Upstream still has no handler for NS-TRY-AGAIN-ERROR and NS-NO-RECOVERY-ERROR around the first connection attempt, the HTTPS probe; the commit widens only the second handler. A contribution would add the handling there. It is a reusable library fix that every process run without a debugger needs, and it is what the fork's change does in the one place where it stands. Prepare it; sending it is a separate decision."
   :EVIDENCE
   ((:TEXT
     "With the real resolver in an empty network namespace, upstream 58a2b2c ends the process at the first connection attempt (DIED, NS-TRY-AGAIN-ERROR); injected NS-TRY-AGAIN-ERROR and NS-NO-RECOVERY-ERROR in that attempt end it too."
     :STATUS :SOURCE-OBSERVED :BASIS
     ("docs/upstream-intake/evidence/58a2b2c/pr15-matrix.tsv (RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15 @7d1adce0, docs/fedwiki-dns-failure/upstream-comparison/evidence/matrix.tsv)"))
    (:TEXT
     "The first handler-case of upstream's MAKE-FEDWIKI names only connection-refused-error and ns-host-not-found-error, and the commit leaves it so."
     :STATUS :MECHANICALLY-DERIVED :BASIS ("HANDLER-PROFILES of the recorded evidence"))
    (:TEXT
     "A patch for that handler would take the same form as the fork's handler list, or the parent class if the maintainers prefer upstream's choice."
     :STATUS :DESIGN-INFERENCE :BASIS ("this ledger, the decision on the class"))
    (:TEXT "The maintainers would accept a change of this kind; not asked." :STATUS :WORKING-HYPOTHESIS :BASIS ("none")))
   :REQUIRED-MIGRATION
   "Write the upstream patch against the first handler-case of MAKE-FEDWIKI (a candidate contribution; docs/hyperdoc-upstream-boundary.md). Until it exists upstream, the fork keeps its reusable extension."
   :VERIFICATION
   ("the first-attempt rows of the matrix turn from DIED to S for an upstream checkout with the patch (docs/fedwiki-dns-failure/upstream-comparison/run-matrix.sh of RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15)")
   :PROPOSED-BY "Claude, from the analysis of RalfBarkow/hyperdoc#15")))
